    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I have made this keybinding that converts a table copied from LibreOffice Calc into a pandoc markdown table:\r\n\r\nThis:\r\n\r\n* Escape `%` characters\r\n* Convert tabs into `|` (column separators)\r\n* Put a `|` at the end of each line\r\n* Put a `|` at the start of each line\r\n* Put the cursor at the first line\r\n* Copy the first line and paste it right after\r\n* Substitute the text in the second line with `---` (define the first line as column headers)\r\n* Select the entire table\r\n* MISSING: Aligns the `|` on top of each other\r\n\r\n```\r\nvim.api.nvim_set_keymap(\r\n  \"n\",\r\n  \"<LocalLeader>t\",\r\n  \"vip:s/%/\\\\%/ge<CR>vip:s/\\t/|/g<CR>vip:s/$/|/<CR>vip:s/^/|/<CR>vipo<Esc>yyp:s/.\\\\{-}|/---|/g<CR>dt|:nohlsearch<CR>vip\",\r\n  {\r\n    noremap = true,\r\n    desc = \"Table: excel2md\"\r\n  }\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe only thing I need is to align the `|` (column separators) on top of each other.\r\n\r\nHow can I do that programmatically with mini.align, by calling a LUA function?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I have made this keybinding that converts a table copied from LibreOffice Calc into a pandoc markdown table:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Escape <code class=\"notranslate\">%</code> characters</li>\n<li>Convert tabs into <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code> (column separators)</li>\n<li>Put a <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code> at the end of each line</li>\n<li>Put a <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code> at the start of each line</li>\n<li>Put the cursor at the first line</li>\n<li>Copy the first line and paste it right after</li>\n<li>Substitute the text in the second line with <code class=\"notranslate\">---</code> (define the first line as column headers)</li>\n<li>Select the entire table</li>\n<li>MISSING: Aligns the <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code> on top of each other</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_set_keymap(\n  &quot;n&quot;,\n  &quot;&lt;LocalLeader&gt;t&quot;,\n  &quot;vip:s/%/\\\\%/ge&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/\\t/|/g&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/$/|/&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/^/|/&lt;CR&gt;vipo&lt;Esc&gt;yyp:s/.\\\\{-}|/---|/g&lt;CR&gt;dt|:nohlsearch&lt;CR&gt;vip&quot;,\n  {\n    noremap = true,\n    desc = &quot;Table: excel2md&quot;\n  }\n)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.api.nvim_set_keymap(\n  \"n\",\n  \"&lt;LocalLeader&gt;t\",\n  \"vip:s/%/\\\\%/ge&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/\\t/|/g&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/$/|/&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/^/|/&lt;CR&gt;vipo&lt;Esc&gt;yyp:s/.\\\\{-}|/---|/g&lt;CR&gt;dt|:nohlsearch&lt;CR&gt;vip\",\n  {\n    noremap = true,\n    desc = \"Table: excel2md\"\n  }\n)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The only thing I need is to align the <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code> (column separators) on top of each other.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How can I do that programmatically with mini.align, by calling a LUA function?</p>",
    "bodyText": "I have made this keybinding that converts a table copied from LibreOffice Calc into a pandoc markdown table:\nThis:\n\nEscape % characters\nConvert tabs into | (column separators)\nPut a | at the end of each line\nPut a | at the start of each line\nPut the cursor at the first line\nCopy the first line and paste it right after\nSubstitute the text in the second line with --- (define the first line as column headers)\nSelect the entire table\nMISSING: Aligns the | on top of each other\n\nvim.api.nvim_set_keymap(\n  \"n\",\n  \"<LocalLeader>t\",\n  \"vip:s/%/\\\\%/ge<CR>vip:s/\\t/|/g<CR>vip:s/$/|/<CR>vip:s/^/|/<CR>vipo<Esc>yyp:s/.\\\\{-}|/---|/g<CR>dt|:nohlsearch<CR>vip\",\n  {\n    noremap = true,\n    desc = \"Table: excel2md\"\n  }\n)\n\nThe only thing I need is to align the | (column separators) on top of each other.\nHow can I do that programmatically with mini.align, by calling a LUA function?",
