            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Might appending something like `ga|vip` work? Here `ga|` aligns restored paragraph visual selection and `vip` again restores visual selection. This would require using `noremap = false` though.\r\n\r\nIf you *have to* use Lua function, take a look at [`MiniAlign.align_strings()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/861c8aa3c68063057707f874e3ae09bf313fd299/doc/mini-align.txt#L551). But using it in this use case (single mapping) doesn't look like straightforward.\r\n\r\nWith example of \"before\" and \"after\" the answer might have been more useful.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Might appending something like <code class=\"notranslate\">ga|vip</code> work? Here <code class=\"notranslate\">ga|</code> aligns restored paragraph visual selection and <code class=\"notranslate\">vip</code> again restores visual selection. This would require using <code class=\"notranslate\">noremap = false</code> though.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you <em>have to</em> use Lua function, take a look at <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/861c8aa3c68063057707f874e3ae09bf313fd299/doc/mini-align.txt#L551\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniAlign.align_strings()</code></a>. But using it in this use case (single mapping) doesn't look like straightforward.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With example of \"before\" and \"after\" the answer might have been more useful.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Might appending something like ga|vip work? Here ga| aligns restored paragraph visual selection and vip again restores visual selection. This would require using noremap = false though.\nIf you have to use Lua function, take a look at MiniAlign.align_strings(). But using it in this use case (single mapping) doesn't look like straightforward.\nWith example of \"before\" and \"after\" the answer might have been more useful.",
