                    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                    "body": "Sorry for the lack of an example.\r\n\r\nHere is an example before:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\t2020\t2021\r\nRevenues\t100\t120\r\nExpenses\t80\t90\r\nMargin\t20\t30\r\nMargin (%)\t20.00%\t25.00%\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere is  the same  example after:\r\n\r\n```\r\n|            | 2020   | 2021   |\r\n| ---        | ---    | ---    |\r\n| Revenues   | 100    | 120    |\r\n| Expenses   | 80     | 90     |\r\n| Margin     | 20     | 30     |\r\n| Margin (%) | 20.00% | 25.00% |\r\n```\r\n\r\n> This would require using noremap = false though.\r\n\r\nYeah the whole point is  that I cannot use `noremap = false`.\r\n\r\nI ended up with this final mapping which uses [godlygeek's tabular](https://github.com/godlygeek/tabular).\r\n\r\nIt would be nice if mini.align would have easy commands like this.\r\n\r\n```\r\nvim.api.nvim_set_keymap(\r\n  \"n\",\r\n  \"<LocalLeader>t\",\r\n  '\"+pvip:s/%/\\\\%/ge<CR>vip:s/\\t/|/g<CR>vip:s/$/|/<CR>vip:s/^/|/<CR>vipo<Esc>yyp:s/.\\\\{-}|/---|/g<CR>dt|:nohlsearch<CR>vip:Tabularize /|<CR>vip<',\r\n  {\r\n    noremap = true,\r\n    desc = \"Paste LOCalc 2 MD\"\r\n  }\r\n)\r\n```\r\n",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry for the lack of an example.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is an example before:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"\t2020\t2021\nRevenues\t100\t120\nExpenses\t80\t90\nMargin\t20\t30\nMargin (%)\t20.00%\t25.00%\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">\t2020\t2021\nRevenues\t100\t120\nExpenses\t80\t90\nMargin\t20\t30\nMargin (%)\t20.00%\t25.00%\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is  the same  example after:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"|            | 2020   | 2021   |\n| ---        | ---    | ---    |\n| Revenues   | 100    | 120    |\n| Expenses   | 80     | 90     |\n| Margin     | 20     | 30     |\n| Margin (%) | 20.00% | 25.00% |\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">|            | 2020   | 2021   |\n| ---        | ---    | ---    |\n| Revenues   | 100    | 120    |\n| Expenses   | 80     | 90     |\n| Margin     | 20     | 30     |\n| Margin (%) | 20.00% | 25.00% |\n</code></pre></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This would require using noremap = false though.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Yeah the whole point is  that I cannot use <code class=\"notranslate\">noremap = false</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I ended up with this final mapping which uses <a href=\"https://github.com/godlygeek/tabular\">godlygeek's tabular</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It would be nice if mini.align would have easy commands like this.</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_set_keymap(\n  &quot;n&quot;,\n  &quot;&lt;LocalLeader&gt;t&quot;,\n  '&quot;+pvip:s/%/\\\\%/ge&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/\\t/|/g&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/$/|/&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/^/|/&lt;CR&gt;vipo&lt;Esc&gt;yyp:s/.\\\\{-}|/---|/g&lt;CR&gt;dt|:nohlsearch&lt;CR&gt;vip:Tabularize /|&lt;CR&gt;vip&lt;',\n  {\n    noremap = true,\n    desc = &quot;Paste LOCalc 2 MD&quot;\n  }\n)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.api.nvim_set_keymap(\n  \"n\",\n  \"&lt;LocalLeader&gt;t\",\n  '\"+pvip:s/%/\\\\%/ge&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/\\t/|/g&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/$/|/&lt;CR&gt;vip:s/^/|/&lt;CR&gt;vipo&lt;Esc&gt;yyp:s/.\\\\{-}|/---|/g&lt;CR&gt;dt|:nohlsearch&lt;CR&gt;vip:Tabularize /|&lt;CR&gt;vip&lt;',\n  {\n    noremap = true,\n    desc = \"Paste LOCalc 2 MD\"\n  }\n)\n</code></pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "Sorry for the lack of an example.\nHere is an example before:\n\t2020\t2021\nRevenues\t100\t120\nExpenses\t80\t90\nMargin\t20\t30\nMargin (%)\t20.00%\t25.00%\n\nHere is  the same  example after:\n|            | 2020   | 2021   |\n| ---        | ---    | ---    |\n| Revenues   | 100    | 120    |\n| Expenses   | 80     | 90     |\n| Margin     | 20     | 30     |\n| Margin (%) | 20.00% | 25.00% |\n\n\nThis would require using noremap = false though.\n\nYeah the whole point is  that I cannot use noremap = false.\nI ended up with this final mapping which uses godlygeek's tabular.\nIt would be nice if mini.align would have easy commands like this.\nvim.api.nvim_set_keymap(\n  \"n\",\n  \"<LocalLeader>t\",\n  '\"+pvip:s/%/\\\\%/ge<CR>vip:s/\\t/|/g<CR>vip:s/$/|/<CR>vip:s/^/|/<CR>vipo<Esc>yyp:s/.\\\\{-}|/---|/g<CR>dt|:nohlsearch<CR>vip:Tabularize /|<CR>vip<',\n  {\n    noremap = true,\n    desc = \"Paste LOCalc 2 MD\"\n  }\n)",
