                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Here is how I would do it with Lua:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal excel_to_md = function()\r\n  -- Initiate marks\r\n  vim.cmd('normal! vip\\27')\r\n\r\n  -- Transform body\r\n  vim.cmd([['<,'>s/%/\\%/ge]])\r\n  vim.cmd([['<,'>s/\\t/|/g]])\r\n  vim.cmd([['<,'>s/$/|/]])\r\n  vim.cmd([['<,'>s/^/|/]])\r\n\r\n  -- Transform header\r\n  vim.cmd('normal! vipo\\27yyp')\r\n  vim.cmd([[s/.\\{-}|/---|/g]])\r\n  vim.cmd('normal! dt|')\r\n\r\n  -- Align (requires 'mini.align')\r\n  local from, to = vim.fn.line(\"'<\"), vim.fn.line(\"'>\")\r\n  local lines = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, from - 1, to, false)\r\n  local aligned_lines = require('mini.align').align_strings(lines, { split_pattern = '|', merge_delimiter = ' ' })\r\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, from - 1, to, false, aligned_lines)\r\n\r\n  -- Cleanup and restore visual selection\r\n  vim.cmd('nohlsearch')\r\n  vim.cmd('normal! vip')\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>yl', excel_to_md, { desc = 'Table: excel2md' })\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlthough it takes much more space, I'd argue that this is at the same time much more readable and understandable.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Here is how I would do it with Lua:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local excel_to_md = function()\n  -- Initiate marks\n  vim.cmd('normal! vip\\27')\n\n  -- Transform body\n  vim.cmd([['&lt;,'&gt;s/%/\\%/ge]])\n  vim.cmd([['&lt;,'&gt;s/\\t/|/g]])\n  vim.cmd([['&lt;,'&gt;s/$/|/]])\n  vim.cmd([['&lt;,'&gt;s/^/|/]])\n\n  -- Transform header\n  vim.cmd('normal! vipo\\27yyp')\n  vim.cmd([[s/.\\{-}|/---|/g]])\n  vim.cmd('normal! dt|')\n\n  -- Align (requires 'mini.align')\n  local from, to = vim.fn.line(&quot;'&lt;&quot;), vim.fn.line(&quot;'&gt;&quot;)\n  local lines = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, from - 1, to, false)\n  local aligned_lines = require('mini.align').align_strings(lines, { split_pattern = '|', merge_delimiter = ' ' })\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, from - 1, to, false, aligned_lines)\n\n  -- Cleanup and restore visual selection\n  vim.cmd('nohlsearch')\n  vim.cmd('normal! vip')\nend\n\nvim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;Leader&gt;yl', excel_to_md, { desc = 'Table: excel2md' })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">excel_to_md</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Initiate marks</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>normal! vip<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\27</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Transform body</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">[[</span>'&lt;,'&gt;s/%/\\%/ge<span class=\"pl-pds\">]]</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">[[</span>'&lt;,'&gt;s/\\t/|/g<span class=\"pl-pds\">]]</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">[[</span>'&lt;,'&gt;s/$/|/<span class=\"pl-pds\">]]</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">[[</span>'&lt;,'&gt;s/^/|/<span class=\"pl-pds\">]]</span></span>)\n\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Transform header</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>normal! vipo<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\27</span>yyp<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">[[</span>s/.\\{-}|/---|/g<span class=\"pl-pds\">]]</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>normal! dt|<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Align (requires 'mini.align')</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">from</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">to</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">line</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>'&lt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>), <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">line</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>'&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">lines</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_buf_get_lines</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">from</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">-</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">to</span>, <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">aligned_lines</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.align<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">align_strings</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">lines</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">split_pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>|<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">merge_delimiter</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span> <span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>})\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_buf_set_lines</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">from</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">-</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">to</span>, <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">aligned_lines</span>)\n\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Cleanup and restore visual selection</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>nohlsearch<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>normal! vip<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Leader&gt;yl<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">excel_to_md</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Table: excel2md<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Although it takes much more space, I'd argue that this is at the same time much more readable and understandable.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Here is how I would do it with Lua:\nlocal excel_to_md = function()\n  -- Initiate marks\n  vim.cmd('normal! vip\\27')\n\n  -- Transform body\n  vim.cmd([['<,'>s/%/\\%/ge]])\n  vim.cmd([['<,'>s/\\t/|/g]])\n  vim.cmd([['<,'>s/$/|/]])\n  vim.cmd([['<,'>s/^/|/]])\n\n  -- Transform header\n  vim.cmd('normal! vipo\\27yyp')\n  vim.cmd([[s/.\\{-}|/---|/g]])\n  vim.cmd('normal! dt|')\n\n  -- Align (requires 'mini.align')\n  local from, to = vim.fn.line(\"'<\"), vim.fn.line(\"'>\")\n  local lines = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, from - 1, to, false)\n  local aligned_lines = require('mini.align').align_strings(lines, { split_pattern = '|', merge_delimiter = ' ' })\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, from - 1, to, false, aligned_lines)\n\n  -- Cleanup and restore visual selection\n  vim.cmd('nohlsearch')\n  vim.cmd('normal! vip')\nend\n\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>yl', excel_to_md, { desc = 'Table: excel2md' })\nAlthough it takes much more space, I'd argue that this is at the same time much more readable and understandable.",
